==============================================================================
 The three 'even graph' counts on K_n (Burnside); the equinumerosity particularity
==============================================================================
  n  A000088(all)  A000568(tourn=Royle-even)  A002854(degree-even=Euler)
  3             4                          2                           2
  4            11                          4                           3
  5            34                         12                           7
  6           156                         56                          16
  7          1044                        456                          54

 A000088 (all graphs):        [4, 11, 34, 156, 1044]  (expect 4,11,34,156,1044)
 A000568 (tournaments/Royle): [2, 4, 12, 56, 456]  (expect 4,12,56,456,6880)
 A002854 (degree-even/Euler): [2, 3, 7, 16, 54]  (expect 3,7,16,54,243)

 PARTICULARITY:
 - tournaments (A000568) = the ODD-ORDER restriction of the all-graph Burnside (= signed cycle
   index P_n(1), THM-587). Royle 2022: also = #Royle-even graphs (an intrinsic property).
 - EULERIAN/degree-even (A002854) = the CYCLE-SPACE Burnside (boundary-zero/F_2). DIFFERENT.
 - all three = 2 at n=3 (coincidence), then diverge: tournaments > Eulerian for n>=4.
 - tournaments are SANDWICHED: A002854 <= A000568 <= A000088 ? True
